1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:04,080
Bitcoin fell almost seven percent from yesterday's local high.

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:06,360
Does that mean you should sell everything?

3
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:08,892
A price drop alone cannot answer that.

4
00:00:09,082 --> 00:00:14,510
In our October 30 snapshot, Bitcoin fell

5
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:17,922
from around $81,900 to $76,300.

6
00:00:17,922 --> 00:00:21,802
It then rebounded toward $78,500.

7
00:00:21,802 --> 00:00:24,392
That's a bounce, not a confirmed bottom.

8
00:00:24,582 --> 00:00:27,142
Technology stocks also weakened.

9
00:00:27,142 --> 00:00:31,642
QQQ closed down about 1.4% on Thursday.

10
00:00:31,642 --> 00:00:34,017
That fits broader risk pressure, but it

11
00:00:34,017 --> 00:00:36,942
doesn't prove what caused every Bitcoin sale.

12
00:00:36,942 --> 00:00:41,517
Liquidations could amplify a drop; verified totals weren't available.

13
00:00:41,707 --> 00:00:44,399
I couldn't verify a current Binance hack

14
00:00:44,399 --> 00:00:46,707
claim in the sources available to me.

15
00:00:46,707 --> 00:00:48,867
Treat it as unconfirmed.

16
00:00:48,867 --> 00:00:51,518
And a hacked exchange would not automatically

17
00:00:51,518 --> 00:00:53,507
mean the Bitcoin network was hacked.

18
00:00:53,507 --> 00:00:56,225
Custody risk and price risk are different.

19
00:00:56,415 --> 00:01:00,277
On the hourly chart, watch the overnight

20
00:01:00,277 --> 00:01:01,915
low around $76,300.

21
00:01:01,915 --> 00:01:04,775
Then watch $79,000 to $80,000.

22
00:01:04,775 --> 00:01:07,495
Reclaiming that area, and holding a retest,

23
00:01:07,495 --> 00:01:09,415
would be an early improvement.

24
00:01:09,415 --> 00:01:11,100
A brief spike isn't enough.

25
00:01:11,290 --> 00:01:14,250
Fresh lows below that overnight floor would

26
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:16,090
keep the downside risk open.

27
00:01:16,090 --> 00:01:19,744
Holding above $80,000 would improve the picture,

28
00:01:19,744 --> 00:01:23,210
with the prior high near $82,000 still overhead.

29
00:01:23,210 --> 00:01:25,725
These are scenarios, not predictions.

30
00:01:25,915 --> 00:01:28,846
Someone holding without leverage for years faces

31
00:01:28,846 --> 00:01:31,917
a different decision from someone using borrowed

32
00:01:31,917 --> 00:01:34,155
money or needing cash soon.

33
00:01:34,155 --> 00:01:37,435
Check your exposure and your custody arrangements.

34
00:01:37,435 --> 00:01:40,087
Don't turn an unverified headline into an

35
00:01:40,087 --> 00:01:41,642
all or nothing decision.

36
